// concatenation (the AAD, its padding, the ciphertext, its padding, the two
// lengths), and building it would copy every byte of the record a second time
// just to hash it. The padding makes each piece a whole number of blocks, so
// absorb is pointed at each in turn, and the ciphertext is read where it lies.
// Building the concatenation took a third of the AEAD's time.
//
