// buys that with an 8 KiB table indexed by a state byte, the textbook
// cache-attack target (Bernstein; Osvik, Shamir and Tromer). It would be worse
// here than in the literature: word regions hold 8 bytes per element, so a
// 256-entry table spans 32 cache lines instead of the 16 a C implementation's
// 4-byte entries take, and one observed line pins five bits of the index
// instead of four. The 256-byte S-box below is a byte region (4 lines, 64
// entries each) and stays the only key-dependent table in the cipher.
